   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "Note",
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Character → rig parts\nWorks best on a **neutral pose** (T- or A-pose, limbs apart) on a plain background. List the parts in **back-to-front draw order**; names are also the SAM3 prompts ('left arm', 'sword', 'tail', 'wing'…). Every visible pixel goes to the front-most part that claims it; leftovers become a 'rest' layer. For each part, klein inpaints only where the part is covered by parts in front of it (e.g. the shoulder under the head), on the original canvas — visible pixels never move or change.\nOutput (output/spritekiln/parts/…): full-canvas aligned PNGs (drop them into Spine/DragonBones/Godot as layers, in order), cropped PNGs, parts.json (box, draw order, pivot guess) and composite.png."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
